          "english_quote": "They stood on the gate’s four sides, with two virgins between each pair of them.",
          "issue": "The translation follows the selected αὐτῶν, but the notes do not disclose the supplied apparatus report that A reads αὐτῆς instead. This is a consequential pronoun alternative in the description of the virgins’ arrangement, not merely a spelling difference. The apparatus attributes support for the working reading to versions; the English documentation leaves that source choice unexplained.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the working translation and add a bounded textual note, for example: “The selected printed Greek reads ‘between them’ (αὐτῶν), which the supplied apparatus reports as supported by versions. A is reported to read αὐτῆς, ‘of/between it,’ changing the pronoun’s reference.” Do not present the reported reading as freshly verified manuscript evidence. Review the proposed note before adoption.",
