          "source_quote": "ὅσα γὰρ οὐ δύνασαι νοῆσαι, μὴ ἐπιχείρει, συνετὸς ὤν",
          "english_quote": "Do not attempt what you cannot understand as though you were wise.",
          "issue": "The English accurately preserves the working text’s inability and prohibition, but its documentation omits the supplied apparatus distinction between printed οὐ δύνασαι and A’s reported οὐδὲ. Footnote c discusses only συνετὸς ὤν, leaving undisclosed the version-supported working wording underlying “cannot understand.”",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep the selected working reading and add a textual note identifying οὐ δύνασαι (‘you cannot’) as the printed reading supported by the versions listed in the supplied apparatus, while A is reported to have οὐδὲ (‘nor/not even’) instead. Explain that this report alone does not establish a complete alternative English sentence; do not silently reconstruct or replace the working text. Review the new note separately.",
