          "english_quote": "Do not try to understand what you cannot grasp as though you were wise.",
          "issue": "The simplified wording preserves the selected prohibition and inability, but the accompanying notes do not disclose that the supplied apparatus reports οὐδὲ for A where the working printed text has οὐ δύνασαι. The existing lexical note addresses the wisdom expression, not this consequential source distinction.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain “cannot grasp” and add a bounded note explaining that the selected printed Greek has ‘you cannot,’ supported by the versions listed in the supplied apparatus, whereas A is reported to have ‘nor/not even.’ Avoid inventing a complete reconstructed alternative sentence from that isolated report. Review the proposed note separately.",
          "severity": "minor"
